    <item>
      <title>Divergence 1.0.301.0</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:23:31 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>1.0.301.0</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.301.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Divergence for Windows 1.0.301.0</h3>
<p><b>This is the first update ever delivered to Windows automatically.</b> Every previous build was handed out by hand.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Trackpad scrolling works.</b> Light scrolling used to produce nothing at all &mdash; small movements were discarded before they reached Windows. Nothing is discarded now, and the speed was tuned by hand until it felt right.</li>
<li><b>The floating session window is gone.</b> It could not track display changes and rendered wrong when you changed resolution or swapped monitors. Session state now lives in the Divergence window, with the tray icon and taskbar button showing a session is running even when that window is closed.</li>
<li><b>Ending a session no longer stops your PC accepting new ones.</b> Previously this was a lockout that could only be undone at the machine itself &mdash; so ending a session from a Mac elsewhere left that PC unreachable. It now ends the session and stays ready for the next one.</li>
<li><b>&ldquo;Stop accepting sessions&rdquo;</b> is the deliberate version of that, and lives in the tray menu where it can only be reached from the machine itself.</li>
</ul>
<p>Scrolling too fast or too slow? It is adjustable without reinstalling and takes effect within a second:<br>
<code>reg add HKCU\Software\HDZCapital\Divergence /v ScrollScale /t REG_DWORD /d 900 /f</code><br>
Lower is faster; the default is 600. Please tell us the number you settle on.</p>
<p>Known: this was tuned on a MacBook trackpad. If you drive Divergence with a <b>mouse wheel</b>, the speed will likely be wrong &mdash; please say so.</p>
<p>Full release notes accompany the installer as <code>RELEASE-NOTE-412edf6.md</code>.</p>
]]></description>
